#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0031 expect=skipped domain=LB
#note "⭐⭐ THE ABSENT-SV CONTROL, and it pins a DELIBERATE behaviour change (PLAN-unplanned-visit-sv-match-tier phase 1). The study carries NO SV dataset at all. BEFORE this plan the rule EXECUTED here and fired once on WEEK 99 through the name tier — measured, this file asserted exactly that and passed. NOW the rule declares Requirements.Datasets: [SV], because `SV._matched_` is unresolvable without it and D89b is binary: declare => SKIP, do not declare => ERROR. There is no third answer, and the ERROR is what this fixture caught. ⇒ a study with no SV gets an auditable SKIP naming SV instead of a TV check decided by visit name alone. ⛔ If this ever reads `violation` again, the declaration has been dropped and every no-SV study is one engine change away from erroring instead."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-2
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 2  | BASELINE
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB | 99 | WEEK 99
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 3 | ALB | 3  |
---

dataset TV label="Trial Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 1 | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | TV | 2 | BASELINE
---
